      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was thinking I\u0027d update the comments for `SelectionPolicy` in the header, but I\u0027m having trouble coming up with the right wording.\n```\nkPreferStillImage may prevent use of the animation features if the input is not rewindable.\n```\n\n? I\u0027m very vague here because e.g. `SkWebpCodec` still copies the stream. It has to, due to its use of `libwebp`. And that has always been its behavior. So no regressions there.\n\nThis bug came up because the switch to Wuffs resulted in a regression - Android used to be able to decode a giant GIF, but the copy ends up using too much memory.\n\nI\u0027m kind of ambivalent about this change at all - it only fixes some cases. If a client used `AnimatedImageDrawable` instead, it would still crash for a similar image.\n\nThe image that sparked the bug is 2.5 GB, with thousands of frames. (It\u0027s probably quite small if you just look at the first frame, but I haven\u0027t.) Not sure why it\u0027s so important to support that, especially when we don\u0027t use most of the info in the file anyway. But it is a regression...\n\nAnd we *are* actually seeing this bug happen. See b/321923587.",
